    midout wide: digit-major slices, four chunks per lane without bank conflicts
    
    The slices are laid out [(v * 16 + q) * 2 + half], so a phase-3b read's
    bank pair is its chunk whatever the digits. Lane t covers chunks
    (t % 16) ^ 4k: a stream's four lanes cover all 16 chunks, and in each
    read a group of 16 lanes reads 16 distinct chunks (with chunks q + 4k
    per lane, four streams' digits decide the banks and the reads
    conflict). The reads of chunks an entry does not keep are no longer
    skipped. Words, masks and records are as before.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

